# Template for the per-database env-files a LOCAL postgres MCP server would consume
# (`docker run --env-file <path>`). Copy once per database, next to this file:
#
#   cp env.template .env_<database>          # then fill in, never commit
#
# The real `.env_*` files are gitignored (`.env*`) and MUST STAY THAT WAY. Three of them were
# committed and pushed to origin/master with live DEV credentials; the accounts were rotated and
# the history rewritten. Do not re-add them, and do not narrow the `.env*` rule in `.gitignore`.
#
# Credentials belong in the file only — never in `opencode.json`, never in a `_note`, never in the
# knowledge base (the KB stores env-var NAMES only, see knowledge-base/README.md §Secrets).

POSTGRES_HOST=
POSTGRES_PORT=5432
POSTGRES_DATABASE=
POSTGRES_USER=
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Shape of the MCP servers that opencode.json deliberately no longer ships
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# The bundle is COPIED into consumer repositories. A database server wired up here would hand
# every consumer's agent a direct SQL channel to databases it has never heard of — the capability
# ADR-0010 removes rather than guards, and a direct contradiction of the bundle's own guardrail
# "No production environments in any test registry". `OpencodeConfigSafetyTest` fails the build if
# such a server, an absolute path, or a filled-in `apiKey` returns to `opencode.json`.
#
# A developer who needs one adds it to a LOCAL override OUTSIDE this repository — never to the
# shipped file. The shape it had, for reference:
#
#   "mcp": {
#     "postgres_<database>": {
#       "type": "local",
#       "command": [
#         "docker", "run", "--rm", "-i",
#         "--env-file", "<absolute path to your .env_<database>>",
#         "us-central1-docker.pkg.dev/database-toolbox/toolbox/toolbox:0.24.0",
#         "--prebuilt", "postgres", "--stdio"
#       ],
#       "enabled": true
#     }
#   }
#
# Requires Docker and access to the GCP image. The IDE server (`jetbrains`) was removed for the
# same reason — its classpath named one machine's IntelliJ installation.
#
# Two rules survive the move:
#   - never point such a server at a production database, local override or not;
#   - the autotests the agent writes reach databases through the SDK's whitelisted datasources,
#     not through an MCP SQL channel. The channel is a developer's debugging tool, never a step
#     in the authoring pipeline.
